# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
#
# The failure mode this guards: the wrong answer is SILENT. Without
# __builtin_add_overflow the sum wraps to INT64_MIN and the program prints a
# large negative number at exit 0 — no diagnostic, no crash, a plausible-looking
# result. Measured on arm64: signed overflow does not trap.
#
# The `1` before the abort also proves the flush: hero_panic calls fflush(stdout)
# before abort(), because six bytes of buffered output were measured surviving
# abort() through a pipe on Darwin.

function main()
    print(1)
    big: int @ 9223372036854775807
    big @ big + 1
    print(big)
